Reused evidence: none. There is no accepted web evidence yet in this thread, and the local prior for 1B was explicitly empty, so I treated it as baseline only.

New evidence:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Constituição da República Federativa do Brasil","publisher":"Presidência da República / Planalto","publication_date":"1988-10-05","url":"https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/constituicao/constituicao.htm","claim":"The President has broad executive authority and the armed forces operate under the President's supreme authority, which defines Bolsonaro's 2022 decision space.","locator":"Art. 84; Art. 142","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative constitutional text; directly states presidential powers and military command relation.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Foundational office-and-authority frame for 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Bolsonaro held this office throughout 2022; the source is institutional rather than personal.","contrary_evidence":["Legal authority does not show how Bolsonaro used it in nuclear or existential-risk matters."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.8","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Emenda Constitucional nº 111","publisher":"Presidência da República / Planalto","publication_date":"2021-09-28","url":"https://planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/constituicao/emendas/emc/emc111.htm","claim":"Presidents elected in 2022 took office on January 1, 2023, so Bolsonaro remained in office through all of 2022.","locator":"Art. 4 and Art. 5","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary constitutional amendment with an explicit transition rule.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly defines the end-of-2022 transition boundary.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional constraint on Bolsonaro's final year in office.","contrary_evidence":["Does not indicate any nuclear-policy choice by Bolsonaro himself."],"lenses":["1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Lei nº 14.222","publisher":"Presidência da República / Planalto","publication_date":"2021-10-15","url":"https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2019-2022/2021/lei/l14222.htm","claim":"Brazil created the National Nuclear Safety Authority (ANSN) as an autonomous federal body to regulate nuclear safety and radiological protection.","locator":"Art. 1","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary federal law; explicit institutional creation and mandate.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Institutional baseline still operative in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Signed in Bolsonaro's administration; institutionally relevant rather than a personal crisis choice.","contrary_evidence":["Creation of an institution does not by itself prove effective safety practice."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Decreto nº 11.142","publisher":"Presidência da República / Planalto","publication_date":"2022-07-21","url":"https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2019-2022/2022/decreto/d11142.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro approved the ANSN's regimental structure and the decree states ANSN must monitor, regulate, and inspect nuclear safety and radiological protection.","locator":"Art. 1 and Art. 2","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential decree with direct operational detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 action within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential signature by Bolsonaro.","contrary_evidence":["Implementation details do not show whether the institution was fully staffed or effective in practice."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brasil participa de Conferência Internacional da AIEA","publisher":"Gabinete de Segurança Institucional da Presidência da República","publication_date":"2022-04-05","url":"https://www.gov.br/gsi/pt-br/centrais-de-conteudo/noticias/2022/brasil-participa-da-conferencia-sobre-a-convencao-de-protecao-fisica-de-material-e-instalacoes-nucleares-na-agencia-internacional-de-energia-atomica-aiea","claim":"Brazil participated in the IAEA verification conference on physical protection of nuclear material and installations, and the final text linked nuclear protection to cyber security and safety culture.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and conference summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Brazilian government report of its own delegation's participation and the conference conclusions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level participation under Bolsonaro's administration; not proof of Bolsonaro's personal authorship.","contrary_evidence":["Participation is precautionary, not proof of an especially dangerous underlying posture."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9"]}
